    "ai.onboardingPrompt" : {
      "comment" : "Pasted into an AI coding assistant; keep the commands and placeholders exactly.",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Please connect this Git repository to YunBox (Git LFS assets go straight to my own Tencent Cloud COS, no server needed) and install the push check.\n\nRepository: %1$@\nCurrent state: %2$@\n%3$@\n\nWork through these steps in order, reading each JSON result before deciding the next step:\n1. In the repository, run `%4$@ doctor --json` to see where things stand; for options you are unsure about, see `%5$@ init --help`.\n2. If the report is missing COS keys (the failed check titled \"COS 密钥\"): stop and ask me to run `%6$@ login` in a terminal myself, or to save them in the YunBox app's Direct COS panel. Do not ask me for the SecretId / SecretKey, and never put keys in command-line arguments, files or the repository.\n3. Run `%7$@ buckets --json` to list the available buckets, and confirm with me which bucket and folder prefix to use (default yunbox/<owner>/<repo>); ask me before creating a new bucket.\n4. Run `%8$@ init --bucket <name-APPID> --region <region> --prefix <prefix> --yes` (add --create for a new bucket).\n5. Run `%9$@ doctor --json` again and make sure nothing fails; if something does, apply its fixes or tell me.\n6. Run `%10$@ hook install` so pre-push checks sizes and push freezes before uploading.\n7. Ask me whether I want push freeze windows; if so, use `%11$@ freeze set \"Mo-Fr 09:00-18:00\"` (add --shared to share it with the team), then confirm with `%12$@ freeze check --json`. See `%13$@ freeze --help` for the syntax.\n8. Show me the changes to .gitattributes and .yunbox/config and let me decide whether to commit them; do not git push, and do not change existing commits."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "请帮我把这个 Git 仓库接入云匣 YunBox（Git LFS 素材直传我自己的腾讯云 COS，不需要服务端），并安装推送检查。\n\n仓库：%1$@\n当前状态：%2$@\n%3$@\n\n按顺序做，每一步先读 JSON 结果再决定下一步：\n1. 在仓库目录运行 `%4$@ doctor --json` 查看现状；不清楚的选项看 `%5$@ init --help`。\n2. 如果报告缺少 COS 密钥（标题为「COS 密钥」的失败项）：停下来，请我自己在终端运行 `%6$@ login`，或在云匣客户端的「COS 直连」面板里保存。不要向我索要 SecretId / SecretKey，也不要把密钥写进命令行参数、文件或仓库。\n3. 运行 `%7$@ buckets --json` 列出可用的 bucket，和我确认用哪个 bucket 和目录前缀（默认 yunbox/<owner>/<repo>）；需要新建 bucket 时先问我。\n4. 运行 `%8$@ init --bucket <名称-APPID> --region <地域> --prefix <前缀> --yes`（新建 bucket 再加 --create）。\n5. 再运行 `%9$@ doctor --json`，确认没有失败项；有失败项时按其中的 fixes 处理或告诉我。\n6. 运行 `%10$@ hook install`，让 pre-push 在上传前检查体积和禁推时段。\n7. 问我是否需要禁推时段；需要时用 `%11$@ freeze set \"Mo-Fr 09:00-18:00\"`（团队共享加 --shared），再用 `%12$@ freeze check --json` 核对。写法见 `%13$@ freeze --help`。\n8. 把 .gitattributes、.yunbox/config 的改动给我看，由我决定是否提交；不要 git push，也不要改动已有提交。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
